WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.890
Henry Cavill's work on Netflix's The Witcher
is fantastic, but the series' supporting cast

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.320
members are memorable too.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.400
Chief among them: Lars Mikkelsen, who plays
the conflicted illusionist Stregobor.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.520
Here's why this guy looks so familiar.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.180
Though he's currently earning rave reviews
for portraying a conniving dark wizard with

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.910
a piercing intellect, The Witcher is hardly
Lars Mikkelsen's first go at breaking bad

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:24.820
on the small screen.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.020
As it happens, the actor has had a pretty
great run playing scheming intellectual sorts

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.280
in movies and TV shows over the years.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.960
As such, we'd wager that many of you who are
certain you've seen Stregobor's face before

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.640
just might be familiar with the genius-level
blackmailing baddie Charles Augustus Magnussen

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.120
one of the most devious villains to ever face
off against Holmes and Watson in the BBC's

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.920
pitch-perfect Sir Arthur Conan Doyle adaptation
Sherlock.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.060
"You just know things.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.440
How does that work?"

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.900
"I just love your little soldier face.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.200
I want to punch it.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.060
Bring it over here a minute."

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.080
Mikkelsen appeared in the episode "His Last
Vow," which found Holmes and Watson on the

00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:09.690
hunt for a collection of deeply personal letters
which were being used as blackmail against

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.040
Lady Elizabeth Smallwood.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:16.160
Their search set Holmes and Watson on a collision
course with Mikkelsen's duplicitous media

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.410
mogul a course that ends with Magnussen ultimately
outwitting Holmes, thus leaving the legendary

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:26.510
sleuth no course of action but to shoot Magnussen
in the head in hopes of saving the lives and

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.840
futures of all those who matter to him.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.780
House of Cards showrunner Beau Willimon was
quick to seize on Mikkelsen's knack for playing

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:39.050
brainy, brutal bad guys when the series was
casting a key supporting role in Netflix's

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.060
breakout drama series.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:45.120
If you count yourself as a fan of House of
Cards, then we're pretty sure a big, fat light

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.130
bulb just went off in your head, because Mikkelsen's
turn as the series' calculating, shamelessly

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.650
manipulative Russian leader Viktor Petrov
remains one of the high points on a show that

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.320
saw dramatic peaks and valleys over its tumultuous
six-season run.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:02.960
Of all the memorable supporting players who
came and went over the course of the series'

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.819
73 episodes, Mikkelsen's potent, 13-episode
arc as Petrov is the one that continues to

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:13.410
stand tallest, if only because the character's
presence was so frequently felt even when

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.700
he wasn't onscreen.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.000
"If people don't like the job you're doing,
they vote you out of office.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.100
If they don't like the job I'm doing, they
topple statues.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:22.960
Blood is spilled.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.300
Chaos takes over."

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.380
It's hard to imagine that Netflix brass wasn't
keenly aware of Mikkelsen's powerful screen

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.560
presence on House of Cards, and it seems possible
that the actor's ability to hold his own against

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.400
some serious dramatic heavy hitters on that
series helped secure his casting on The Witcher.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.980
If you've never taken a moment to check in
with either House of Cards or Sherlock, it's

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.560
entirely possible you don't recognize Mikkelsen's
face at all.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.300
But even if that is the case, the actor's
voice might ring a bell.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.640
You might recognize his performance from a
certain galaxy far, far away, specifically

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.560
the Star Wars franchise's compelling animated
series Star Wars Rebels.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.500
Rebels follows the adventures of a starship
crew who bravely stand up to the Galactic

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.160
Empire, which is busy traversing the galaxy
stamping out the remnants of the Jedi Order.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:17.130
Joining a star-studded cast of talent including
the likes of David Oyelowo, Clancy Brown,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:21.060
and more, Mikkelsen lent his voice to the
show by stepping into the boots of the feared

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:26.650
Imperial leader Grand Admiral Thrawn, who
frequently tormented the ragtag group of rebels

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.720
throughout the series.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.340
Mikkelsen has a number of projects in the
works; to name just a couple, he'll be featured

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.670
in the upcoming crime drama The Knife Thrower,
and on the Danish small screen serial Grow,

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.100
which is currently shooting.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.319
In the meantime, though, he's enjoying the
raised profile that comes with his supporting

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.740
role on The Witcher.

